 \psz9\linex0\endnhere\sectdefaultcl {\footer \pard\plain \s17\nowidctlpar\widctlpar\tqc\tx4320\tqr\tx8640\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {\field{\*\fldinst { DATE \\@ "dd-MM-yy" }}{\fldrslt {\lang1024 09-06-99}}}{     }{\field{\*\fldinst {\cgrid0  FILENAME }}{\fldrslt {\lang1024\cgrid0 proposal.doc}}}{
\par }}{\*\pnseclvl1\pnucrm\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxta .}}{\*\pnseclvl2\pnucltr\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxta .}}{\*\pnseclvl3\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxta .}}{\*\pnseclvl4\pnlcltr\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxta )}}{\*\pnseclvl5\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}{\*\pnseclvl6\pnlcltr\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}{\*\pnseclvl7\pnlcrm\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}{\*\pnseclvl8\pnlcltr\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}{\*\pnseclvl9\pnlcrm\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}\pard\plain \s15\qc\nowidctlpar\widctlpar\adjustright \b\cgrid AÏZI SURVEY PROPOSAL
\par \pard\plain \nowidctlpar\widctlpar\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {
\par 
\par There are three Aïzi languages spoken by people in twelve villages on the Ebrié Lagoon of Côte d\rquote Ivoire. Two of the languages (representing about 8000 people) belong to the Kru language family, and the third (4000 people) is a Kwa language. There is reportedly very little mutual comprehension between the three speech forms, to the point that a lingua franca is used between members of the different speech communities. In the past, Adioukrou was used as the lingua franca. Today, the younger generation uses French and it appears that French proficiency is increasing.
\par 
\par The primary goal of this survey is to determine if French is the language best suited to serve the needs of the Aïzi church. There are two secondary goals. 
\par 
\par 1) Anticipating the possibility that French is the best choice, we will be prepared to put the church and community leaders in touch with the appropriate local agency (ies) to help promote the use of the French scriptures. 
\par 
\par 2) Anticipating the possibility that French is not adequate, we will evaluate the community interest in (and probable commitment to) involvement in a language project, either in Adioukrou or in one, two or three of the Aïzi languages. In this case, additional research would also be warranted, beyond the scope of this survey, to pursue the questions of Adioukrou proficiency and further linguistic analysis of Aïzi. It seems most likely that any projects in Aïzi would be undertaken by the Adioukrou translation team once the Old Testament translation is completed.
\par 
\par 
\par Research Questions
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\widctlpar\tx360\adjustright {1a) \tab What is the level of French proficiency?
\par 1b) \tab Is the level of French proficiency stable or changing?
\par 1c) \tab Is French proficiency homogeneous?
\par 2)\tab How are Aïzi churches currently using the French language and French materials?
\par 3)\tab What are the Aïzi communities\rquote  attitudes toward French, especially within the church?
\par 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\widctlpar\adjustright {
\par Methods
